# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so never put
# a real value here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
#
# A variable already exported in the shell wins over the file, so an explicit
# `export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=...` always overrides what is written here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick a provider. The first three blocks call a vendor's HTTP API and need a
# key here. The fourth needs nothing here at all: it hands the prompt to a
# locally running opencode server, which already holds the account's
# credential. That is the cheap arm -- a run costs whatever the subscription
# already costs -- and it is also the one that reports no token usage, so the
# cost table prints n/a for it rather than a zero. Run the arms you need to
# account for over a vendor API, and the rest through opencode.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- straight to DeepSeek (the default provider) ---------------------------
# Key: https://platform.deepseek.com/
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# --- or through OpenRouter -------------------------------------------------
# Same chat-completions shape, different host and different model ids: on
# OpenRouter a model is "vendor/model", not a bare name. Select it with
#   ssrefuse judge --provider openrouter --model <vendor/model>
# or leave OPENROUTER_MODEL set here and omit --model.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# --- or any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint -------------------------------
#SSREFUSE_LLM_BASE_URL=
#SSREFUSE_LLM_API_KEY_ENV=SSREFUSE_LLM_API_KEY
#SSREFUSE_LLM_API_KEY=
#SSREFUSE_LLM_MODEL=

# --- or through a locally running opencode server --------------------------
# No key goes here: the server holds the account's OAuth token and refreshes
# it, and this project authenticates to the server over loopback with the
# password opencode wrote to ~/.config/opencode/service.json.
#
#   opencode service start          # must be running
#   opencode models                 # the ids, as `provider/model`
#   ssrefuse judge --provider opencode --model opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash
#
# The provider half of the id is the billing tier and is not cosmetic:
# `opencode-go/...` draws on an OpenCode Go subscription, the `opencode/...`
# mirror of the same model is pay-per-token, and `...-free` has its own daily
# ceiling that returns "Free usage limit reached" once spent.
#
# Both variables below are optional. The server address is discovered from
# `opencode service status`, which is the right default because the port is
# assigned at startup.
#SSREFUSE_OPENCODE_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:0000
#SSREFUSE_OPENCODE_MODEL=opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash
#SSREFUSE_OPENCODE_SERVICE_CONFIG=~/.config/opencode/service.json
#
# What this transport cannot tell you, which is why it is not the default:
#   token usage          absent -- reported as n/a, never as 0
#   reasoning_content    absent -- the chain of thought does not come back
#   temperature          not settable; --temperature is not sent
#   JSON mode            unavailable; the answer is parsed out of prose
#   thinking `off`       has no variant, so that arm needs --provider deepseek

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model ids and thinking mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checked against the provider changelog on 2026-10-20. Check again before a
# submission: a model id is a version, and a run against a retired name is a
# run that did not happen.
#
#   deepseek-flash    V4.1 Flash, the current default here
#   deepseek-v4-pro   the larger one
#
# `deepseek-chat` and `deepseek-reasoner` are the OLD names. They selected
# non-thinking and thinking mode respectively, and were scheduled for
# retirement on 2026-07-24. Thinking is a request parameter now:
#
#   ssrefuse judge --effort none    # parameter not sent at all
#   ssrefuse judge --effort low|high|max
#
# That is the ablation axis: one model, the thinking budget moved. Holding the
# model fixed is what lets a difference in the numbers have one cause.
